1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the original code, documentation and other material whose
copyright owners make it available under this license, including contributions
explicitly submitted and accepted under this license. Separately identified
third-party material is not Software under this definition.

"You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this license.

"Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for, directed toward, or in support
of commercial advantage or monetary compensation, whether directly or indirectly.
It includes internal business operations, commercial product research or
development, paid consulting, sale or licensing of products, and provision of
commercial hosted or network services using the Software. Making a service free
to its immediate users does not make a commercially operated service
noncommercial. Nonprofit status alone does not exempt a commercial activity.
Unpaid personal study, teaching and research unrelated to commercial advantage
may qualify as noncommercial use.

"Combined Work" means a program or service incorporating, embedding, statically
or dynamically linking the Software, or containing adaptations of it. A wrapper
or companion component specifically designed to integrate the Software as part
of one program or service is included, including integration across a process
or network boundary. Independent programs merely stored alongside the Software,
general-purpose operating systems and development tools are not included merely
for that reason. Data, circuits and other outputs produced by running the
Software are not covered merely because the Software produced them, unless they
contain or adapt a substantial portion of the Software itself.

"Complete Source" means the preferred form for modifying a work, including its
covered components, interface definitions, and scripts and instructions needed
to build, install and run it. Separately licensed third-party dependencies may
be identified by exact versions, publicly accessible source locations and their
applicable licenses instead of being copied into the source release. Private
keys, access credentials and personal or confidential input data must not be
included; provide instructions for supplying those separately.

