3. No closed-source use; public source requirement

ArcTN official-engine exception: solely loading an unmodified Light/Heavy
binary supplied by the company under its separate terms does not require
disclosing that binary's proprietary implementation. This exception covers
only that official engine implementation, not other modifications or closed
integration code. All conditions on the Software, including noncommercial
use and source availability of covered modifications, continue to apply.
This exception does not itself grant a license to the engine binary.

You may not use the Software in a closed-source Combined Work. Before running,
deploying, providing access to or distributing a modified version of the
Software or a Combined Work, You must make its Complete Source freely available
to the public, without registration, payment or a confidentiality obligation.
This requirement applies to internal use and network services as well as
distribution. Publish the covered modifications and integration code under
this same license, granting recipients the same rights. Unmodified Software
already available publicly under this license satisfies the source requirement
for that unmodified Software. Merely publishing a binary, patches without the
applicable base source, or a description of an implementation is insufficient.

Identify each released or deployed version and provide a working source link
with distributed copies and in the interface or documentation of a service.
Keep the applicable Complete Source publicly available for as long as You use
or provide the work and for at least three years after Your last use, provision
or distribution of that version. Preserve this license and copyright notices,
and clearly identify modifications and their dates. Do not impose additional
restrictions that prevent recipients exercising the rights granted here.

